course: dictionary
lesson: 8567
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, look at the context: the words and sentences around it. «Scatter» can mean to throw things so they land in many places, to run off in different directions, or a small spread of things.
explain: «The farmer scattered seeds across the field.» Try the meaning in the sentence: the seeds were thrown, not run away with, so the first meaning fits. Always check your meaning by putting it back into the sentence.
explain: «The sky is blue because the gas in the air scatters blue light.» Here scatter means the air sends the light off in many directions. The same word can change its meaning, so the context tells you which one to use.
fact: Some words have more than one meaning.
fact: Context clues help you choose the right meaning.
fact: «Scatter» means to throw or drop things so they land in many different places.
fact: «Scatter» can also mean people or animals running away quickly in different directions, as when birds scatter when something frightens them.
fact: A «scatter» is a small number of things spread out over an area, and a scatter graph shows dots spread over a chart.
exercise: «The farmer scattered seeds across the field.» What does scattered mean here? | *To throw so they land in many places | To count them carefully | To run away in fear | To gather into one heap
exercise: «When the dog barked, the pigeons scattered.» What does scattered mean here? | *Ran away quickly in different directions | Fell asleep in one place | Sang loudly together | Flew into one tree and stayed
exercise: Ella drew a scatter graph to check whether two things are linked. What is a scatter graph? | *A chart with dots spread out to show if two things are linked | A map of the stars | A cake with sprinkles | A list of names in order
test: «Families scattered the ashes of their loved one at sea.» What does scattered mean here? | Washed them clean | *Spread them over an area | Put them in a box | Lost them
test: Maya says scatter is only ever a verb. Who is right? | Maya is wrong, because it means very hungry | Maya is right, because it is a colour | Maya is right, because it is always a verb | *Maya is wrong: a scatter can also be a noun, meaning a small number of things spread over an area
exam: «The Sun's light is basically white; our air scatters blue light.» What does scatters mean here? | *Sends light off in many directions | Hides | Makes the light stronger | Turns the light into darkness
